==Upgrading==
Players can bring the quiver to [[Ava]], along with [[Ava's assembler]], [[Ava's accumulator]], or their [[max cape]] equivalents, to apply the same ammunition-saving effect of her devices to the quiver. Doing so will '''not''' consume the devices. Upgrading the quiver with the [[ranging cape]] will only provide the effect of Ava's accumulator; the quiver must be combined with Ava's assembler to receive its effect. This upgrade applies to '''all''' quivers the player owns, now and in the future - if a player loses all of their quivers and obtains a new one, they will '''not''' need to go back to Ava to reobtain the ammo-saving effect. The interaction between Ava devices and metal torsos '''does not''' carry over when adding the Ava effects to the Dizana's quiver.

Blessing the quiver retains any ammo-saving effects used on an unblessed [[Dizana's quiver]].

==Wilderness==
If the player dies below level 20 [[Wilderness]], it will remain in the player's inventory, but will be unusable and require 400,000 coins to repair. The killer will receive 400,000 coins as well as any ammo that the quiver was holding, though any sunfire charges will not be lost. Above level 20 Wilderness, a lesser amount will be dropped, along with any ammo in the quiver; the quiver itself and its charges will be destroyed in the process. The quiver - along with its [[Dizana's max cape|max cape variant]] - can be locked by bringing it, along with a [[Trouver parchment|Trouver Parchment]] and 500,000 coins, to [[Perdu]]. This will allow the quiver to be kept upon death to another player above level 20 Wilderness.

